        "resolved_model": "glm-5.3-flash",
        "verdict": "REQUEST_CHANGES",
        "confidence": 7,
        "critical_issues": [],
        "major_concerns": [
          "Release bump is PATCH (1.8.9→1.8.10) while this sprint raises engines.node to >=20.19.0 and adds the prisma.config.ts packaging requirement (DD-009). Under SemVer an engine-floor raise is at least MINOR; consumers on ^1.8.x silently receive a change that can break Node <20.19 runtimes, and the visible CHANGELOG diff records no Node-floor line (hunk context hides lines 7-9 — verify and add if absent). Cheap pre-push fix: re-version via sync-version.sh to 1.9.0 and add 'requires Node >= 20.19.0' to the 1.8.10/1.9.0 entry."
        ],
        "minor_concerns": [
          "AC-003-02: committed @intent references .sprint-state/.../ac003-timing-and-memory-evidence.md, which is gitignored — cold 3654 ms / p95 figures are not durably in-repo (learnings.md carries only the warm numbers). Commit a summary so the reference resolves post-clone; the bench re-buy is already #150.",
          "Invariant-test holes: a multi-line `import {\n…} from '…/generated/prisma'` evades the import-type check, and the `(cli.match(/prisma\\.config\\.ts/g)).length >= 2` proxy can pass-while-broken (comments count; behavior unproven). Overall it is fail-loud drift-pinning, acceptable now; tighten later.",
          "No evidence exercises PrismaPg + real PostgreSQL (suite is PGlite-only). The adapter wiring is a v6-existing baseline and PGlite is real PG16, so shipping on Playwright evidence per call #4 is acceptable; add a one-off real-PG /health smoke at SHIP to close AC-005-02 fully.",
          "Wording drift: CHANGELOG says the generate step is 'in all PR jobs' while AGENTS.md (correctly) says 6 consuming jobs, security-scan excluded."
        ],
        "consensus_ratio": 0.8,
        "summary": "Calls 1-4 are defensible: replacing the parallel-suite wall-clock assertion with deterministic mechanism invariants is correct (230→2700 ms with unchanged code is scheduler noise, not regression); re-anchoring governance ACs from gitignored artifacts to committed invariants is faithful; Playwright-only browser evidence is shippable given the pre-existing, user-approved #156 hazard and the 0-message incident; template hardening is sound. The blocking gap is the release: engines.node >=20.19.0 plus prisma.config.ts packaging shipped as PATCH 1.8.10 misleads ^1.8.x consumers and the visible changelog omits the floor. Re-version to 1.9.0 with an explicit Node-floor entry before push. Minors: gitignored evidence file referenced by committed @intent; multi-line import bypass; real-PG smoke at SHIP."
      }
    ],
